## Summary

Shipped the SwiftUI parity of the web AI-Off Contract HOC (`components/ai/withAiFeature.tsx`, ADR-015) as **9 files** under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/withAiFeature.*`:

- **`.Adapter`** — surface meta (slug `withAiFeature`), connectivity/status/mode enums, registry guard (reuses the canonical 57-id `AIFeatureRegistry` — DRY), `AiFeatureGate` (verbatim port of `useAiEnabled`'s fail-closed truth table incl. the unknown-id throw), and the marker builder (`ai-feature-<id>` = web `data-testid`; `displayName` parity).
- **`.Projection`** — pure `resolve` → `presented | withdrawn`.
- **`.Model`** — P1/S10 i18n facade, P1/S11 telemetry seam (`view.opened`), P1/S8 source seam (Live/InMemory), and `@Observable WithAiFeatureGateModel` (lazy once-only `view.opened` only when presented; one-shot stale auto-refresh).
- **`.swift`** — generic `WithAiFeature<Inner: View>` HOC + `.withAiFeature(_:gate:)` modifier (debug-assert on unknown id mirroring the web throw; fail-closed in release).
- **`.Views`** (marker modifier), **`.strings`**, **`.Previews`**, **`.Tests` + `.ModelTests`**.

**Parity-honest note:** the web HOC is transparent (enabled → marked inner; else → `null`); I did *not* invent skeleton/error/stale chrome it doesn't have. All non-enabled verdicts render nothing.

